  message: "FIX DEPLOYED in PR #2042 (dev 5c85a1d0c3), pending_validation until the next full-suite cron's self-claims-gate step is green. Three dated module_completeness grants at the exact slots named: datetime.timezone (python.yaml), textual.widgets.Select and hypergumbo_core.scip._generated.scip_pb2 (docs/io-primitives-overlays/hypergumbo-self.yaml); SECURITY.md's untyped-receiver paragraph re-measured (10,395 of 14,024). BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (production path, lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/self_audit_11032026/after_grants_*): verify-claims on the patched tree rc 3, 18 of 18 confirmed_with_caveats, opaque_boundary back on every claim; scripts/check-self-claims-drift against the committed snapshot: OK, 18 unchanged, so the September snapshot was NOT re-recorded; scripts/check-claims-coverage 0; smart-test 11,277 passed (the one red, test_check_mode_passes_on_committed_state, was SECURITY.md regenerated after the run started; green on re-run). BISECT: at 1443c2da57, the parent of #2036's 3e4b895996, all 18 were ALREADY inconclusive on scip_pb2 alone (ab_pregabak_1443c2da57.json, 12m27s); #2036 added the two from-imported slots. The scip_pb2 introducing commit is not bisected further. Statement re-scoped to the snapshot half; the guard-parity half is WI-jizam. NOT covered: the same cron's self-tree-validation red (id_format|warning 2 > 0) has a separate cause and keeps the cron red after this fix."  # 427c
